Falsifies `program_argument_contract::verification::the_builder_and_the_parser_round_trip_two_arguments`.

The defect: `push` writes the length prefix and then zeros where the argument's bytes belong, so
the page parses with the right count and lengths but the wrong bytes.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(read.next(), Some(arguments[0]))`, on any first
argument of one byte or more that is not all zeros.

diff --git a/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@
         let length = u32::try_from(argument.len()).map_err(|_| PushRefused::TooLong)?;
         let at = HEADER_BYTES + self.used;
         self.page[at..at + LENGTH_PREFIX_BYTES].copy_from_slice(&length.to_le_bytes());
-        self.page[at + LENGTH_PREFIX_BYTES..at + need].copy_from_slice(argument);
+        self.page[at + LENGTH_PREFIX_BYTES..at + need].fill(0);
         self.used += need;
         self.count += 1;
         Ok(())
